Applied by tools/build-toolchain.sh to bebbo/newlib-cygwin commit
0909ae9abc18b38595425143e7a63d9e2fc31174.  Commit 120371e changed __argv
from an array to a pointer to fix amiga-gcc issue #8, but kept two writes
through __argv before assigning it any storage.  The resulting crt0 writes a
longword through address zero before main().

Keep __argv as the pointer expected by __nocommandline.c and give its initial
Shell/Workbench values a real two-entry vector.  __nocommandline.c may replace
the pointer later with its parsed vector exactly as before.

diff --git a/newlib/libc/sys/amigaos/crt0.c b/newlib/libc/sys/amigaos/crt0.c
index 81ffc44..1b8116a 100644
--- a/newlib/libc/sys/amigaos/crt0.c
+++ b/newlib/libc/sys/amigaos/crt0.c
@@ -34,2 +34,3 @@
-char ** __argv = {0, 0};
+static char * __argv_storage[2] = {0, 0};
+char ** __argv = __argv_storage;
 int __argc;
